From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: keep LOS indication while digital PHY is down

LOS can briefly deassert without PHY_READY while fibre is absent. That is
not proof of a usable optical link. Do not alternate the PON registration
indicator with LOS merely because that raw bit changes. This affects only
the front-panel policy, not the GPON state machine or optical registers.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
@@ -1268,4 +1268,6 @@
-	} else if (READ_ONCE(priv->led_optical_known) &&
-		   READ_ONCE(priv->led_los)) {
+	} else if ((READ_ONCE(priv->led_optical_known) &&
+		    READ_ONCE(priv->led_los)) ||
+		   (READ_ONCE(priv->phy_link_known) &&
+		    !READ_ONCE(priv->phy_link_up))) {
 		los = AIROHA_XPON_LED_BLINK;
 	} else if (READ_ONCE(priv->mac_enabled)) {
